          "explanation": "Correct! $\\mathcal{L}\\{y'\\} = sY(s) - y(0)$ and $\\mathcal{L}\\{y''\\} = s^2Y(s) - sy(0) - y'(0)$. These formulas incorporate the initial conditions.",
          "insight": "The Laplace transform converts derivatives to algebra, bringing in initial conditions automatically."
