    "fullSolution": "**Solve:** $y'' + 4y' + 3y = 0$, $y(0) = 2$, $y'(0) = -1$\\n\\n**Laplace transform:**\\n$$\\mathcal{L}\\{y''\\} + 4\\mathcal{L}\\{y'\\} + 3\\mathcal{L}\\{y\\} = 0$$\\n$$[s^2Y - sy(0) - y'(0)] + 4[sY - y(0)] + 3Y = 0$$\\n$$[s^2Y - 2s + 1] + 4[sY - 2] + 3Y = 0$$\\n$$(s^2 + 4s + 3)Y = 2s + 9$$\\n\\n**Solve for Y(s):**\\n$$Y(s) = \\frac{2s + 9}{s^2 + 4s + 3} = \\frac{2s + 9}{(s+1)(s+3)}$$\\n\\n**Partial fractions:** $Y = \\frac{A}{s+1} + \\frac{B}{s+3}$\\n\\n$2s + 9 = A(s+3) + B(s+1)$\\n- $s = -1$: $7 = 2A \\Rightarrow A = 7/2$\\n- $s = -3$: $3 = -2B \\Rightarrow B = -3/2$\\n\\n$$Y(s) = \\frac{7/2}{s+1} - \\frac{3/2}{s+3}$$\\n\\n**Inverse Laplace:**\\n$$y(t) = \\frac{7}{2}e^{-t} - \\frac{3}{2}e^{-3t}$$\\n\\nVerify: $y(0) = 7/2 - 3/2 = 2$ \u2713",
